  "tagline": "Retired Apache SQL-on-Hadoop data warehouse engine with its own distributed executor; moved to the Attic.",
  "description": "Apache Tajo was a distributed relational data warehouse for Hadoop that started at Korea University. Instead of compiling SQL to MapReduce like early Hive, it ran its own distributed execution engine with a cost-based optimizer, supported standard SQL with complex joins, and queried columnar and row-format files in HDFS or S3, with a JDBC driver for BI tools. It became an Apache top-level project in March 2014, but development faded after 0.11.3 in 2016; the project retired in September 2020 and moved to the Apache Attic in April 2021. Trino, Spark SQL or Hive on Tez cover its use cases today.",
